  "term": "perspective theory",
  "definition": "In this historical psychology usage, perspective theory is a type of explanation for geometrical-optical illusions. In Baldwin’s summary, it is grouped with theories that treat such illusions as variants of broader accounts of how visual perception produces mistaken appearances.",
